Since the decimal repeats after 3 digits, the multiplication factor 1000 should be used. After multiplying (1) by 1000, we get the equation which is aligned with the decimal point in equation (1) as follows: {eq}\begin{aligned} 1000x &= 4054.\overline{054} \\ {/eq}

